.TH JICHI 1 "2026\-08\-22" "jichi 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jichi \- terminal AI coding agent (C89 reimplementation of the Continue CLI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jichi
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIprompt\fR]
.br
.B jichi
.I command
[\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jichi
is an interactive (TUI) and headless AI coding agent. With no prompt on a
terminal it starts a REPL; with
.B \-p
or piped stdin it runs one turn and prints the reply. It streams from
OpenAI\- or Anthropic\-style model servers, calls tools (read/write/edit files,
run commands, search, git, MCP, \&...), and gates mutating tools behind a
permission prompt.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-print <prompt>
Headless mode: print the reply and exit
.TP
.B \-\-config <path>
Use the given JSON config file
.TP
.B \-\-config\-json <s>
Use inline JSON as the whole config (self\-contained runs;
visible in `ps` \-\- use apiKeyEnv, not a literal key)
.TP
.B \-\-config\-json\-b64 <b64>
Base64 of the inline config (quoting\-safe transport)
.TP
.B \-\-config\-json \-
Read the config JSON from stdin (alias \-\-config\-stdin;
keeps it out of `ps`; prompt must then use \-p/\-\-prompt\-b64)
.TP
.B \-\-prompt\-b64 <b64>
Base64 of the prompt text (multiline/quote\-safe)
.TP
.B \-\-design <file>
Inject a design/spec doc as the authoritative plan for the task (alias \-\-spec)
.TP
.B \-\-model <sel>
Select a configured model (name/index/id substring), or a raw id
on the active model if nothing matches
.TP
.B \-\-plan
Start in plan mode (investigate, propose a plan, change nothing)
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Start in auto mode (run approved tools without asking)
.TP
.B \-\-readonly
Disable mutating tools
.TP
.B \-\-path\-fence/\-\-no\-path\-fence
Force the workspace path containment fence on/off (default: auto = on in \-\-auto)
.TP
.B \-\-prompt\-cache/\-\-no\-prompt\-cache
Force prompt caching on/off (default: auto = on)
.TP
.B \-\-cost\-model/\-\-no\-cost\-model
Tell the model its output caps and what follows (default: auto = on when caching is off)
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-context/\-\-no\-auto\-context
Auto\-retrieve relevant code/docs into each turn (default: off)
.TP
.B \-\-learn\-on\-stop/\-\-no\-learn\-on\-stop
Draft lessons via the mentor after a completed \-\-auto run (default: off)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hooks
Disable configured lifecycle hooks for this run
.TP
.B \-\-output\-style <name>
Activate a custom output style (.jichi/output\-styles/<name>.md)
.TP
.B \-\-language <lang>
Answer in this natural language (e.g. Japanese, Deutsch; config "language")
.TP
.B \-\-image <path>
Attach an image to the prompt (repeatable; needs a vision model). In a message, @photo.png / @img:<path> also attach.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-continue
Resume the most recent session for this directory (alias: \-\-resume)
.TP
.B \-\-session <id>
Resume a specific session (id or unambiguous prefix; see `ls`)
.TP
.B \-\-all
With ls / \-\-continue: every project, not just this directory
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging
.TP
.B \-\-voice / \-\-no\-voice
Speak replies, approval prompts and errors aloud (needs an
audio\-role model + sound.play; off by default)
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet, \-\-silent
Minimal output: only essential info (errors still shown)
.TP
.B \-\-output <fmt>
Output format: text (default), json (one object), or jsonl (streaming events)
.TP
.B \-\-heartbeat <secs>
With \-\-output jsonl: emit a periodic "heartbeat" event
while a model call is in flight (0 = off; for supervisors)
.TP
.B \-\-color/\-\-no\-color
Force ANSI color on/off (default: auto; honors NO_COLOR)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stdin
Do not read piped stdin as/with the prompt
.TP
.B \-\-no\-session
Do not save this run as a session
.TP
.B \-\-lite
Low\-resource profile (lean defaults for RAM/CPU/disk;
alias \-\-low\-memory; config: "lowResource")
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lite
Force the normal profile (wins over the config key
and the low\-RAM auto\-detection)
.TP
.B \-\-reindex
Rebuild the index cache from scratch
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat all following args as the prompt
.SS Autonomous envelope (bounds an unsupervised run; implies \-\-auto in headless mode)
.TP
.B \-\-verify <cmd>
Run <cmd> when the agent finishes; it must pass (exit 0)
.TP
.B \-\-with\-rules
attempt: load the project's AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md into the graded run
(off by default \-\- a big rules file dominated every call: M309)
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-retries <n>
Fix\-forward attempts before rollback (default 3)
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-every <n>
Run the verifier every <n> tool calls mid\-turn (bank green / feed failures back)
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-timeout <dur>
Kill the verifier if it runs longer (e.g. 5m)
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-baseline
Run the verifier once at start (records if the tree is already broken)
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-kind <invariant|goal>
Declare what the verifier asserts: an invariant (green before the work) or a goal (red until the work lands).
Declaring arms the start probe, which CHECKS the declaration: a goal gate that already passes forces nothing (config "verifyKind")
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rollback
On failure, leave the workspace as\-is instead of reverting
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-scope
With \-\-edit\-scope, also forbid run_terminal_command (no shell escape)
.TP
.B \-\-privileged\-commands <ask|deny|allow>
Policy for model\-issued sudo/doas/pkexec (default ask; config "privilegedCommands")
.TP
.B \-\-kinetic\-commands <ask|deny|allow>
Policy for model\-issued physical actuation (default ask; config "kineticCommands")
.TP
.B \-\-revert\-out\-of\-scope
Restore files changed outside the edit scope at turn end (config "revertOutOfScope")
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-green
Refuse a passing verify if the run changed a file outside the edit scope (config "strictGreen")
.TP
.B \-\-lease
MODE Concurrent runs on one workspace: warn (default) | fail | off (M431e)
.TP
.B \-\-budget\-panel
Give the agent a periodic budget reading with its spend RATE (off by default; config "budgetPanel")
.TP
.B \-\-preserve\-discarded
Commit the tree a rollback would throw away, under refs/jichi/discarded/ (config "preserveDiscarded")
.TP
.B \-\-parallel\-verify
Verify each parallel write\-child's worktree before merging it (config "parallelVerify")
.TP
.B \-\-budget\-tokens <n>
Token cap for the run (e.g. 200k, 1m)
.TP
.B \-\-deadline <dur>
Wall\-clock cap (e.g. 30s, 20m, 2h)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-tool\-calls <n>
Cap on tool calls ATTEMPTED (a
gate\-refused call still counts)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-reads <n>
Cap on read\-category tool calls (prevents over\-reading)
.TP
.B \-\-context\-limit <n>
Context budget in tokens (sizes the system\-prompt fit + compaction; use when the model's real context is smaller than its declared contextLength)
.TP
.B \-\-tool\-profile <p>
auto | core | full \-\- advertise the lean core tool set on a small\-context model (auto: core when context is small or \-\-lite)
.TP
.B \-\-edit\-scope <glob>
Restrict file edits to a path glob (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-reference\-root <path>
Allow READS under this external root with the fence on (repeatable; writes stay in\-workspace)
.TP
.B \-\-journal <path|\->
Audit log path (default ~/.jichi.d/runs/<id>.jsonl; \- disables)
.TP
.B \-\-control [path]
Open a mid\-run control socket (default ~/.jichi.d/control/<pid>.sock;
steer with `jichi control <sock> status|inject|pause|resume|abort|mode`)
.SS Event logging / telemetry (opt\-in; for analyzing jichi itself)
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level <tier>
off | metrics | full (default off; full adds prompt/response content)
.TP
.B \-\-log <path|\->
Telemetry JSONL path (default ~/.jichi.d/telemetry/<id>.jsonl; \- disables;
implies metrics if no \-\-log\-level)
