.SS Safety off-switches
These turn OFF a guard that is otherwise on. Every one of them was accepted by the
parser and documented nowhere at all until M539 -- not in this page, not in
.BR "jichi \-\-help" .
A fence an operator cannot discover is a fence they cannot reason about, so this
subsection admits no exemption: a flag that disables a guard belongs here.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-preserve\-discarded
Do not keep the state an
.B undo
throws away. Normally the discarded work tree is preserved and
.B undo
prints a
.B "jichi recover <hash>"
handle for it; with this, the revert is final.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rollback
On failure, leave the workspace as it stands instead of reverting it. The
autonomous envelope's automatic rollback is what makes an unsupervised run
recoverable; this removes it.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-revert\-out\-of\-scope
Do not revert edits that fall outside
.BR \-\-edit\-scope .
The scope is still reported, but no longer enforced by reverting.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-self\-review
Skip the self-review pass at the end of an autonomous run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-strict\-green
Accept a verify command's success without the strict-green checks that catch a
gate passing for the wrong reason (a moved assertion, a skipped suite).
.TP
.B \-\-config\-editable
Allow the model to write the configuration file through the
.B config set
path. Off by default: a model that can edit its own config can edit its own
fences.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation on
.BR "checkpoints gc" ,
which deletes checkpoint stores. There is no undo for a pruned store.
.SS Setup, export and diagnostics
Flags that belong to one subcommand, or exist for diagnosing jichi itself.
.TP
.B \-\-provider \fI<name>\fR, \-\-profile \fI<name>\fR, \-\-key\-env \fI<VAR>\fR, \-\-lang \fI<lang>\fR, \-\-config\-target \fI<path>\fR, \-\-from \fI<path>\fR
Non-interactive answers for
.BR "jichi setup" :
the provider, the profile, the environment variable holding the API key, the
answer language, where to write the config, and a config to import.
.B \-\-from
is the same as
.BR \-\-import ,
and
.B \-\-lang
the same as
.BR \-\-language .
.TP
.B \-\-out \fI<path>\fR
Write
.BR "jichi export" 's
output to a file rather than stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-record
For
.BR "jichi attempt" :
append the graded result to
.IR .jichi/progress.jsonl .
.TP
.B \-\-review
Ask for a review pass over the result.
.TP
.B \-\-fuzzy\-edit
Force the whitespace/anchor fallback for
.B edit_file
on (the opposite of
.BR \-\-no\-fuzzy\-edit ).
.TP
.B \-\-parallel\-verify, \-\-no\-parallel\-verify
Run the envelope's verify commands concurrently, or serially.
.TP
.B \-\-non\-interactive
Never prompt; fail instead of asking. For cron and CI.
.TP
.B \-\-mem\-budget \fI<MB>\fR
Advisory memory ceiling for the low-resource profile.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-budget\-panel
Suppress the TUI's budget panel.
.TP
.B \-\-dump\-requests \fI<dir>\fR
Write every outgoing request body to
.IR <dir> .
A debugging aid: request bodies contain your prompt, your files and, if a config
inlines one, your key.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Commands
.TP
.B ls [\-\-all]
List saved sessions (this project; \-\-all for every project)
.TP
.B prune [\-\-keep N] [\-\-older\-than DUR] [\-\-dry\-run]
Delete old sessions (both criteria must agree; \-\-dry\-run lists)
.TP
.B export [id] [\-\-html]
Export a session transcript (Markdown, \-\-html, or \-\-output
json for a structured projection); \-o <file>
.TP
.B index [\-\-reindex]
Build/update the codebase search index
.TP
.B docs [index|search]
List/index/search external documentation sources
.TP
.B setup
Guided project setup: role preset \-> assets + config +
start\-script + validation (interactive; \-\-list, \-\-preset)
`\-\-api\-base <URL>` sets the endpoint a locally hosted or
gateway model needs (the flag form of the wizard's
apiBase question);
`\-\-context\-length <tokens|auto>` records the model's
window (a number stays offline; `auto` asks the server,
which only a LiteLLM gateway answers);
`setup \-\-import <continue|opencode config>` converts an
existing config into a jichi config + .jichi/ tree;
`\-\-journey`/`\-\-machine`/`\-\-stance` <name> layer onto it
(setup asks for both; \-\-preset <journey> alone still works);
`setup \-\-advisor` asks the configured model for tailored
recommendations (writes .jichi/setup.advice.md);
`setup \-\-from\-global` seeds the project config from
~/.jichi (\-\-inherit <keys> copies only some);
`setup \-\-onboard` scaffolds + drafts a propose\-only
project analysis + tutorial (W6)
.TP
.B init [pack ...]
Scaffold .jichi/ assets (agents, skills, commands, AGENTS.md);
.TP
.B \-\-list packs, \-\-global, \-\-force, \-\-dry\-run
.TP
.B embed "text"
Print an embedding (uses the embed model)
.TP
.B rerank "q" "doc"...
Score documents against a query
.TP
.B doctor
Check config, keys, server reachability, MCP/LSP, git
(\-\-output json for a machine\-readable report;
.TP
.B \-\-live
makes ONE real request that advertises a trivial
tool, to confirm tool calling works end to end
.TP
.B \-\-unattended
judges the config as an unattended\-loop
posture and exits 1 on an unsafe one)
.TP
.B config [path|show|validate]
Name the config file(s) in effect, summarise the
resolved settings, or confirm it parsed; `config set <key>
<value>` and `config telemetry <level>` edit it when
configEditable is on
.TP
.B assign <spec.md>
Render a machine\-checkable assignment for its audience
.TP
.B hint <spec.md> [N]
Print rung N of the spec's hint ladder (default 1)
.TP
.B grade <spec.md>
Run the spec's verify command and score pass/fail
(\-\-expect\-fail: authoring check \-\- exit 0 iff the gate
is RED on the untouched tree; a green one is HOLLOW)
.TP
.B attempt <spec.md>
Let a learner solve one assignment in an isolated worktree,
graded by its verify (\-\-agent <profile> picks a tier;
.TP
.B \-\-budget\-tokens/\-\-deadline/\-\-max\-tool\-calls
bound it;
a green verify with test\-assertion edits reports TAINTED,
exit 1 \-\- \-\-keep\-worktree keeps the sandbox for review)
.TP
.B dream [path]
Propose\-only reflection over telemetry \-> a dated draft
.TP
.B workflow <spec.json>
Run a deterministic multi\-agent pipeline (map \-> synthesize)
.TP
.B improve [specs\-dir]
Reflect + grade a spec suite; track the pass\-rate over time
(\-\-attempt: let the agent try each failure in an isolated
worktree and re\-grade \-\- your tree is never touched)
.TP
.B models
List configured models, roles, fallback, and live reachability
.TP
.B benchmark [path]
Score a config against the built\-in checks (offline)
.TP
.B board [add|move|done|phase] ...
Show or edit the persistent kanban board (.jichi/board.json)
.TP
.B packages [recommend]
List the setup presets (role recipes) `setup \-\-preset` accepts;
`recommend` suggests one from what is in the project
.TP
.B timeouts
Show the model\-call timeouts in effect for the active model
.TP
.B mcp [resources|read <uri>|prompts|prompt <name>|call <tool> [json]]
Connect to configured MCP servers; list tools, or use one
.TP
.B skills
List available agent skills
.TP
.B agents
List discovered agent profiles (.jichi/agents)
.TP
.B commands
List custom slash commands (.jichi/commands)
.TP
.B output\-styles
List output styles (.jichi/output\-styles)
.TP
.B rules
Print the resolved project rules (AGENTS.md chain)
