.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version and exit
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print this help and exit
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
Keys available while composing a prompt in the TUI. Two of them make a model
call and are easy to confuse; they differ in what they do to your line.
.TP
.B Tab
Complete the token under the cursor: a slash-command, a model name, a session
id, a mode, or an
.I @path
reference. Offline and deterministic.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-G
Suggest how to finish the current line ("ghost text", shown dim after the
cursor).
.B Tab
accepts it and appends it to your line; any other key dismisses it. Uses the
.B autocomplete
role model. Whether you get a continuation rather than an answer depends on that
model \(em see
.IR docs/AUTOCOMPLETE.md .
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Q
Ask whether the request you are composing is clear enough to act on. One short
line is
.B printed
below your prompt, labelled
.IR advice: ,
and your input is never modified. Replies
.I looks clear
when nothing needs deciding. Uses the active chat model.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-R
Reverse\-search your input history.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-A, Ctrl\-E
Start / end of line.
.B Ctrl\-U, Ctrl\-K
kill to start / end;
.B Ctrl\-W
kill the previous word.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-L
Clear the screen.
.B Ctrl\-C
cancels the current turn or clears the line;
.B Ctrl\-D
exits on an empty line.
.TP
.B \\ (trailing backslash)
Continue the prompt on the next line. Pasted multi\-line blocks are also kept as
one logical line.
