.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit codes are a
.B stable
interface: see
.IR docs/EMBEDDING.md .
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime error. See stderr, or the
.B done.error
field under
.BR "\-\-output json" .
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (SIGINT).
.TP
.B 143
Terminated (SIGTERM), shut down gracefully -- the session is saved and teardown
runs. Absent from this page until M539, while
.BR "jichi describe" ,
.BR "jichi \-\-help" ,
.I docs/EMBEDDING.md
and
.I docs/SCRIPTING.md
all listed it: a supervisor reading only the man page would treat a clean
SIGTERM shutdown as an unknown failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.jichi
Default config file.
.TP
.B .jichi/
Project-local commands, agents, skills, and memory.
.TP
.B ~/.jichi.d/sessions/
Saved sessions.
.SH SEE ALSO
The bundled README.md, TUTORIAL.md, and docs/ directory.
